{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n \\\"runPostCommitBoundaryAdvance|advanceDecision|executeBoundaryAdvance|view_boundary|visibility|post-commit-advance|tool_result_summary|abridged|full content in record|advance\\\" packages/lhc/src packages/lhc/test packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact -g '\"'!artifacts/**'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts:298:    // sums and visibility budgets validated — throws naming the violation.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/team-impl-log.md:6:- Current Story: 04-tool-result-visibility\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/team-impl-log.md:36:- 04-tool-result-visibility\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/team-impl-log.md:54:  - spec-deviation-2 (view_boundary migration seed uses strftime): accepted-risk (benign) — approved via same ruling; one-time static-SQL seed, production writers use injected clock\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/team-impl-log.md:145:- Anti-shim themes: fixture states via production drains only (never hand-written derived_form rows); no test-only advance() surface; sweep never waits; materialize renders pull output only; PI format fixture must come from a real PI session with provenance.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/team-impl-log.md:148:- Per story: story-orchestrate validate → run (background; 1-2 quick checks then persistent 5-min Monitor until terminal) → review final package → fix routing if needed → impl-lead runs story gate (green-verify) + verify-all → baseline check (never lower) → receipt → story commit → advance.\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-turns.test.ts:560:    const resultA = formOf(filePath, \"m3\", \"tool_result_summary\")?.content;\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-turns.test.ts:562:    const resultB = formOf(filePath, \"m5\", \"tool_result_summary\")?.content;\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/test-plan.md:40:| TC-4.3 | 4.5 | view-boundary | monster turn: advance enters open turn but the whole-message protected set stays full (newest results joined to ≥ floor; oversized-newest protected alone); turn's text messages all full | architecture-risk: floor arithmetic |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/test-plan.md:43:| TC-4.6 | 4.9 | view-boundary | injected advance failure: intake succeeds, boundary unmoved, status shows over-max; next batch heals | injection seam; also asserts poke still fired (drain ran) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/test-plan.md:61:| advance/poke seam isolation | view-boundary | TC-4.6's sibling: a *throwing* advance must not eat the queue poke (drain still runs), and a failing poke must not block the advance. Ordering pinned in design Flow 4. |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/test-plan.md:65:| CLI intake advances boundary | cli-process-view | The design's both-modes advance rule proven at the process boundary: spawned CLI intake on an over-max thread → subsequent `view pull` shows flipped results, `view status` shows zone ≤ target. Guards the seam-install class (a createSdk-only install would pass every in-process test and fail this one). |\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:208:    expect(result.value.dropped.map(formKey)).toEqual([\"message/m3/tool_result_summary\"]);\npackages/lhc/test/epic-fix-02.test.ts:387:      (f) => f.subjectId === \"m5\" && f.form === \"tool_result_summary\",\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:5:This epic defines the complete requirements for thread views: the assembled working context a harness actually loads. It covers pulling the active view, smart compact, the readiness sweep, tool-result visibility in the live tail, and the two render targets. It serves as the source of truth for the Tech Lead's design work.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:17:Two cost realities shape everything here. First, the pull sits on the hot path between a user's action and a model call, so it must be reads and deterministic assembly only — derivation already happened, in Epic 02, off this path. Second, harnesses cache the prompt prefix; every byte that changes above the newest content costs real money. The MVP's per-turn tool-result truncation churned the cache every turn. This design changes the prompt only in planned, batched steps: a compact (rare, explicit), or a tool-result visibility advance (only under budget pressure).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:36:4. **Tool-result visibility** — one boundary marker per thread; tool results behind it render short, ahead of it render full; advances in batches under budget pressure only; never moves backward.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:58:- The tool-result visibility boundary: position marker, max/target budgets, protected floor, compact reset, post-commit advance step with non-blocking failure semantics\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:81:- One writing process per thread file (tech arch); the boundary advance and compact both write under that assumption.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:86:The harness asks for the current context. The pull reads the active view's stored band snapshot (if a compact has run), reads the tail — messages after the compact point — applies the visibility boundary to tail tool results, and returns the assembled message array. Reads and deterministic formatting only. The pull writes nothing and decides nothing; every judgment call (band membership, visibility, gap handling) was made earlier by a compact, a boundary advance, or Epic 02's derivations.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:100:- **AC-1.7**: Two pulls with no intervening intake, boundary advance, or compact return byte-identical output.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:108:- **TC-1.5** (AC-1.6): Delete a tail message, pull → message absent. Delete a message banded in the snapshot, pull → band unchanged; status read shows the record changed (next-compact visibility).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:112:Compact is an explicit operation on the thread-view surface. Nothing in core triggers it: the harness, the operator, or a future monitor calls it, and the status read gives any caller the numbers to decide with. The operation takes a named profile or explicit parameters — lower bound and band percentages — validates them, and builds the new view: select which chunks and turns fall into which band (recency gradient: brief for the oldest, then detailed, then smoothed turns, then the full tail), render each band from stored artifacts, and atomically replace the active view — arrangement, rendered snapshot, compact point, config used, and gaps in one transaction. The visibility boundary resets to the compact point. By default the compact runs the readiness sweep (Flow 3) first.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:123:- **AC-2.6**: The compact replaces the active view atomically: band arrangement, rendered snapshot, compact point, config used, and gaps land in one transaction; the visibility boundary resets to the compact point in the same transaction. A crash mid-compact leaves the previous view intact and serving.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:125:- **AC-2.8**: The status read returns: tail size against the configured trigger threshold and a compact recommendation; derivation counts by state (pending, retrying, failed, blocked); the active view's degraded-entry and gap counts; and the visibility zone's token sum against its max — reads only, callable any time, no side effects.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:166:Old tool results are the tail's bloat: one agentic turn can dump a hundred thousand tokens of file reads and build output. The MVP re-decided every result's visibility on every message, churning the prompt cache every turn. This design replaces that with one marker per thread and a log-rotation policy: nothing happens until the full-visibility zone outgrows its budget, then one batched advance, then quiet again.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:168:The rule set, complete: tool results at-or-behind the boundary render short (Epic 02's summary when usable, deterministic truncation otherwise); tool results ahead of it render full; nothing else is ever affected — prompts, assistant text, and thinking always render full. After an intake batch commits, the advance check runs as a thread-view maintenance step, triggered through the SDK's post-commit seam (Epic 02's onCommit pattern) — automatic, never a host-remembered call, and outside the intake transaction, so intake's outcome never depends on it. One indexed sum measures the full-zone tool tokens; if it exceeds the max budget, the boundary advances oldest-first until the zone is at-or-under the target budget; otherwise nothing happens. A failed advance leaves the boundary unchanged and the over-budget condition visible in the status read; the next batch's check re-evaluates the same condition, so the debt is bounded by one batch. The boundary never advances into the protected floor — the most recent stretch of tool output stays full even mid-monster-turn — and never moves backward: a flipped result stays flipped. A compact resets the boundary to the compact point, because the old tail just became bands.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:170:Because the advance is oldest-first, closed turns age out before the open turn's work; the boundary only eats into the open turn when that turn alone exceeds the budget, and even then the floor protects its most recent reads. Budgets — max, target, floor — are configuration with defaults, not architecture.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:174:- **AC-4.1**: Each thread carries one visibility boundary. Tail tool results at-or-behind it render the short form; ahead of it, full. Non-tool-result content is never affected by the boundary.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:176:- **AC-4.3**: The boundary advances only when, after an intake batch commits, the full-zone tool-result token sum exceeds the max budget; the advance moves oldest-first until the sum is at-or-under the target. Below max, the boundary does not move and rendered bytes do not change.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:177:- **AC-4.4**: The advance is deterministic and mechanical: token sums from stored per-message estimates, no inference, no provider calls.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:178:- **AC-4.5**: The boundary never advances into the protected set: the newest whole tool-result messages, joined newest-backward until their combined tokens first reach or exceed the floor, render full — even when the open turn alone exceeds the max, and even when the newest single result exceeds the floor by itself (it is protected alone; the zone may legally sit above target until later batches or a compact create room).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:182:- **AC-4.9**: The advance check runs after intake commit, outside the intake transaction, triggered through the SDK's post-commit seam — never by a separate host call. Intake's outcome never depends on it. A failed advance leaves the boundary unchanged with the over-budget condition visible in the status read; the next successful check re-evaluates and advances.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:186:- **TC-4.1** (AC-4.3): Intake tool results totaling under max → boundary unmoved; pulls byte-identical across batches. Cross max with one more batch → boundary advances once to target; exactly one batch of results flipped, oldest-first; next under-max batch → no movement.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:188:- **TC-4.3** (AC-4.5): Single monster turn: tool results exceeding max within one open turn → boundary advances into the turn but stops at the protected set; the newest whole results (combined tokens ≥ floor) render full; oversized-newest leg: a single result larger than the floor is protected alone; the turn's own text messages all render full.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:189:- **TC-4.4** (AC-4.6, AC-4.7): After an advance, intake small batches → flipped results stay flipped (no backward motion); compact → boundary equals compact point; fresh tail renders full.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:191:- **TC-4.6** (AC-4.9): Inject a failure at the advance seam (test seam from Story 0); intake a batch that crosses max → intake reports success and all messages committed; boundary unchanged; status read shows the zone sum over max. Clear the injection; intake another batch → the advance lands at target.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:225:**Visibility boundary** (one per thread): a source event order position (the compact point's coordinate system); budgets (max, target, floor) resolved from config; written only by the post-commit advance step and the compact reset.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:235:**Status read**: tail tokens, configured trigger threshold, compact recommendation; derivation counts by state (pending, retrying, failed, blocked); active-view health (degraded-entry count, gap count, built-at); visibility-zone token sum against its max.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:244:- **Cache stability:** band snapshot bytes are stable between compacts, unconditionally. Tail changes are append-only except boundary advances, which are batched and budget-triggered. No per-turn churn path exists.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:245:- **No inference in this epic:** pull, compact, sweep, materialize, boundary advance — no Epic 03 operation invokes a provider. Tests observe zero provider calls from these operations; test setups may drain Epic 02 work (which exercises the provider fake) to reach the states under test.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:248:- **Concurrency:** one writing process per thread file (inherited); compact and boundary advance both write under that regime; pulls are read-only and safe alongside.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:252:1. Post-commit seam wiring: the boundary advance and Epic 02's queue poke share the onCommit seam — pin their ordering and isolation (a failed advance must not eat the poke, and vice versa).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:257:6. Sweep requeue history: is a cross-invocation cap or backoff needed for forms that fail transiently again and again, or is receipt visibility enough for v1?\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:270:**Scope in:** migration for the view and boundary tables; profile config parsing and band-sum/budget validation; the advance-seam test injection point; the derived-thread fixture — a recorded thread with Epic 02 artifacts in known states (ready, failed-transient, failed-permanent, blocked) plus a canonical-corruption variant (Epic 01 fixture pattern), for every later story to compact against.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:318:**Scope in:** boundary marker storage; post-commit advance step through the SDK seam; budget sum + oldest-first advance to target; protected floor; never-backward; compact reset wiring (the reset transaction landed in Story 2; this story proves it end-to-end); short-form rendering in pulls; advance-failure semantics and status visibility.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:319:**Scope out:** any change to band rendering; any host-called advance surface.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:344:PRD Feature 3 ACs map: AC-3.1 → Flow 1 (AC-1.1, 1.2); AC-3.2 → AC-1.4, AC-1.7 plus the cache NFR; AC-3.3 → AC-2.4; AC-3.4 → AC-2.5; AC-3.5 → AC-4.3 (eligibility is positional — older than where the boundary will land; activation is the batched advance); AC-3.6 → AC-4.2; AC-3.7 → AC-5.3; AC-3.8 → Flow 3 (AC-3.1, 3.3, 3.5).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:381:- [x] Settled design decisions from the planning conversation are encoded: snapshot views (no live mutation visibility), no force-refresh, explicit-call compact with profiles, sweep-never-waits with transient-only requeue, log-rotation boundary, two render targets\npackages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts:112:      workItemId: \"w-m2-tool_result_summary-v1\",\npackages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts:114:      kind: \"tool_result_summary\",\npackages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts:130:        workItemId: \"w-m2-tool_result_summary-v1\",\npackages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts:132:        kind: \"tool_result_summary\",\npackages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts:313:        { work_item_id: \"w-m3-tool_result_summary-v1\", status: \"queued\" },\npackages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts:439:      tool_result_summary: { owner: \"messages\", sourceRefKey: \"messageId\" },\npackages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts:457:      \"tool_result_summary\",\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:5:The visibility boundary: post-commit advance through the SDK seam in both host modes, whole-message floor protection, never-backward, compact reset, short-form rendering.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:15:- `boundary.ts` advance per tech design §Deterministic Algorithms: post-commit indexed sum (deleted-filtered) → over max ⇒ advance oldest-first to target, stopping at the whole-message protected set (newest results joined to ≥ floor; oversized-newest protected alone) → write position\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:16:- Wiring per the Flow 4 DD: intake-stream registers the advance on `ctx.onCommit` (advance first, poke second, throw-isolated both directions); runs in **both host modes**; budgets resolve through the per-instance seam with defaults below SDK\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:22:**Scope out:** any change to band rendering; any host-called advance surface (no public advance operation exists — the seam is the only writer besides compact reset).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:29:- **AC-4.1**: Each thread carries one visibility boundary. Tail tool results at-or-behind it render the short form; ahead of it, full. Non-tool-result content is never affected by the boundary.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:32:- **AC-4.3**: The boundary advances only when, after an intake batch commits, the full-zone tool-result token sum exceeds the max budget; the advance moves oldest-first until the sum is at-or-under the target. Below max, the boundary does not move and rendered bytes do not change.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:33:  - **TC-4.1** (AC-4.3): Intake tool results totaling under max → boundary unmoved; pulls byte-identical across batches. Cross max with one more batch → boundary advances once to target; exactly one batch of results flipped, oldest-first; next under-max batch → no movement.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:34:- **AC-4.4**: The advance is deterministic and mechanical: token sums from stored per-message estimates, no inference, no provider calls.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:35:- **AC-4.5**: The boundary never advances into the protected set: the newest whole tool-result messages, joined newest-backward until their combined tokens first reach or exceed the floor, render full — even when the open turn alone exceeds the max, and even when the newest single result exceeds the floor by itself (it is protected alone; the zone may legally sit above target until later batches or a compact create room).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:36:  - **TC-4.3** (AC-4.5): Single monster turn: tool results exceeding max within one open turn → boundary advances into the turn but stops at the protected set; the newest whole results (combined tokens ≥ floor) render full; oversized-newest leg: a single result larger than the floor is protected alone; the turn's own text messages all render full.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:39:  - **TC-4.4** (AC-4.6, AC-4.7): After an advance, intake small batches → flipped results stay flipped (no backward motion); compact → boundary equals compact point; fresh tail renders full.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:42:- **AC-4.9**: The advance check runs after intake commit, outside the intake transaction, triggered through the SDK's post-commit seam — never by a separate host call. Intake's outcome never depends on it. A failed advance leaves the boundary unchanged with the over-budget condition visible in the status read; the next successful check re-evaluates and advances.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:43:  - **TC-4.6** (AC-4.9): Inject a failure at the advance seam (test seam from Story 0); intake a batch that crosses max → intake reports success and all messages committed; boundary unchanged; status read shows the zone sum over max. Clear the injection; intake another batch → the advance lands at target.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:51:The boundary is the view's one self-acting piece — everything else changes by explicit call. Its writers are exactly two: this story's post-commit advance and Story 2's compact reset (already landed; this story proves the reset end-to-end). The advance rides the same `ctx.onCommit` seam as Epic 02's queue poke, registered by intake-stream — which makes this the story that introduces the sanctioned intake→thread-view surface import and the domain graph's first cycle (both pre-cleared in the design and the check-boundaries script per Story 0's DoD).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:55:Pure decision first: `advanceDecision(zone summary, budgets) → new position | none` as a pure function, driven by Boundary G1's trajectory golden including the floor legs — all the arithmetic risk, no IO. Then the write path (own short transaction), then the seam wiring (registration order, throw isolation), then the rendering integration (short forms in pulls — `render.ts` already selects by position from Story 1; this story makes positions *move*). Red: decision function throws `NotImplementedError`; seam registered but no-op.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:61:| `src/domains/thread-view/internal/boundary.ts` | `advanceDecision` (pure); advance executor (sum → decide → write, own transaction); the shared deleted-filtered SUM (built in Story 1, consumed here) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:62:| `src/domains/intake-stream/index.ts` | the one registration: advance first, poke second, advance wrapped (catch + diagnose, never throw into flush, never eat the poke) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:63:| budget resolution | instance seam (`SdkViewConfig.visibility`) with defaults below SDK — same mechanism as the poke's instance resolution, no new channel |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:72:| Short-form ladder + `abridged` marker | tech-design.md L198, L202–229 |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:83:| TC-4.3 | `view-boundary.test.ts` | monster turn: advance enters open turn, stops at protected set (≥ floor by whole messages); oversized-newest protected alone; text messages all full |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:86:| TC-4.6 | `view-boundary.test.ts` | injected advance failure: intake succeeds + messages committed; position unchanged; status zone > max; **poke still fired (drain ran)**; cleared → next batch lands at target |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:90:Seam isolation, both directions (a throwing advance never eats the poke — TC-4.6 carries the assert; a failing poke never blocks the advance — separate leg). Both-modes proof in-process: manual-mode SDK intake advances, background-mode SDK intake advances. The process-boundary CLI leg is Story 5's (named debt in DoD). Supplemental golden: **Boundary G1 trajectory** in `view-select-golden.test.ts` — committed positions after each scripted batch, floor legs included (not a TC; hand-derived expectations per the goldens discipline).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:94:The advance's sum and `status`'s zone sum are the same query by construction (Story 1 note) — if they ever diverge, TC-4.6's status assertion is the canary. \"Visible in status\" is structural, not stored: no failure flag row exists; status recomputes the sum live. The advance writes in its own short transaction *after* intake's commit — never inside intake's transaction (AC-4.9's isolation is the point). Flip granularity is whole messages, oldest-first by `source_event_order`; the protected-set walk is newest-backward. Budgets resolve per-instance: a CLI invocation and a background extension on the same thread may briefly hold different budgets — the boundary only moves forward, so the worst case is an earlier flip than the larger config would choose, which is benign and not worth a coordination mechanism.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:98:No host-called advance surface may exist — if a test needs an advance, it intakes a batch (the seam is the only trigger; a test-only `advance()` export would be the forgettable-nudge pattern reborn). The G1 golden's expected positions are hand-derived from the design rules before implementation, same discipline as Story 2's goldens. TC-4.6's injection uses the Story 0 facility's named post-commit point — not a mock of `boundary.ts`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:116:- [ ] Both-modes rule proven in-process (manual-mode SDK intake advances; background-mode SDK intake advances) — process-boundary CLI leg deferred to Story 5 with a named debt comment\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:117:- [ ] Status zone sum verified equal to advance-decision sum on the same state (deleted-filter consistency)\npackages/lhc/src/shared/derivation.ts:14:  | \"tool_result_summary\"\npackages/lhc/src/shared/derivation.ts:159:  view?: SdkViewConfig; // Epic 03: profiles, visibility budgets, compact threshold\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:1:// Epic 03 Story 4: the visibility boundary (TC-4.1–4.6, the seam-isolation\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:3:// status-sum/advance-sum equality check). Every advance here fires through a\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:4:// REAL `intake.messageEvents` commit — no host-called advance surface exists\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:38:  setViewInjectionHook(\"post-commit-advance\", null);\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:43:function visSdk(view: SdkViewConfig = { visibility: BUDGETS }, mode: \"manual\" | \"background\" = \"manual\"): Lhc {\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:108:function abridgedCount(messages: ReadonlyArray<{ content: string }>): number {\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:109:  return messages.filter((m) => m.content.startsWith(\"[tool result · \") && m.content.includes(\" · abridged]\"))\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:135:    expect(abridgedCount(afterSecond.value.messages)).toBe(0);\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:137:    // The crossing batch (zone 120 > 100): one advance to target — the three\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:148:    expect(abridgedCount(crossed.value.messages)).toBe(3);\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:150:    // Oldest-first: precisely the first three results render abridged.\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:151:    const abridgedIds = results\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:154:    expect(abridgedIds).toEqual(results.slice(0, 3).map((r) => r.messageId));\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:156:    // DoD: status's zone sum equals the advance's decision sum on the same\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:164:    expect(status.value.visibility.zoneTokens).toBe(expectedZone);\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:165:    expect(status.value.visibility.zoneTokens).toBe(60);\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:176:    const sdk = createSdk({ provider: double, mode: \"manual\", view: { visibility: BUDGETS } });\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:189:    // First tool_result_summary execution fails non-retryably (r1's — queue\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:191:    double.failKind(\"tool_result_summary\", 1, {\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:206:      r1.forms?.find((f) => f.form === \"tool_result_summary\")?.state,\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:209:      (f) => f.form === \"tool_result_summary\" && f.state === \"ready\",\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:224:    // prefix, exact dropped-count marker, abridged marker, record pointer.\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:226:      `[tool result · read_file · abridged]\\n${tokens(60).slice(0, 200)}… [truncated 39 chars] [full content in record §${r1.messageId}]`,\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:230:      `[tool result · read_file · abridged]\\n${r2Summary} [full content in record §${r2.messageId}]`,\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:240:describe(\"TC-4.3 (AC-4.5): monster turn — the advance enters the open turn but stops at the whole-message protected set\", () => {\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:270:    expect(abridgedCount(pulled.value.messages)).toBe(3); // r0, m1, m2\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:282:    expect(status.value.visibility.zoneTokens).toBe(65);\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:308:    expect(abridgedCount(pulled.value.messages)).toBe(3);\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:313:    expect(status.value.visibility.zoneTokens).toBe(80); // above target until room appears\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:323:    const advanced = results[2]?.sourceEventOrder ?? 0;\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:324:    expect(awa